L1: #!/usr/bin/env node
L2: // Two suites, answering two different questions.
L3: //
L4: //   --suite offline   Does the PIPELINE still work? Replays a recorded sweep
L5: //                     through the committed bundle and asserts the invariants
L6: //                     that matter downstream. Deterministic, no network, runs
L7: //                     in CI on every push.
L8: //
L9: //   --suite network   Do the UPSTREAMS still speak the shape we parse? Five
L10: //                     public APIs, none of them ours, all free to change a
L11: //                     field name without telling anyone. These are canaries,
L12: //                     not gates: they are opt-in, and a red run means "go look
L13: //                     at the API", not "the code is broken".
L14: //
L15: // Keeping them apart is the point. A network assertion inside the unit gate
L16: // turns every Overpass outage into a failed build, and after the third false
L17: // alarm nobody reads the gate any more.
